{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EKksPq3yrda1yqYsH65ZFh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Resource interface\n2\t\n3\tTool resource arguments contain URI-encoded relative resource identifiers.\n4\tReference objects carry decoded logical locators. The provider API is shared by\n5\tother clients and accepts URI-encoded absolute locators; it decodes one layer\n6\tbefore storage normalization. Percent signs can be part of literal stored names.\n7\tSlashes separate nested resources. A project member can read only resources in\n8\tthat project and tenant. The provider has service-wide data access; callers are\n9\tnot granted project access by the provider adapter itself.\n10\t\n11\tThe local provider implements its entire identifier interpretation here. It does\n12\tnot forward requests to an unknown network provider. Native filesystems, symbolic\n13\tlinks and HTTP redirects are not involved. The public module supports separately\n14\tconstructed local clients; the default registry remains the caller-facing API.\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ac62724-9b8b-487c-84fb-0f28bfe4ebb2","uuid":"faccc90b-b288-4643-8539-23c32744900b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:26:17.780Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-review-nnazxmth/repo/docs/provider.md","content":"# Resource interface\n\nTool resource arguments contain URI-encoded relative resource identifiers.\nReference objects carry decoded logical locators. The provider API is shared by\nother clients and accepts URI-encoded absolute locators; it decodes one layer\nbefore storage normalization. Percent signs can be part of literal stored names.\nSlashes separate nested resources. A project member can read only resources in\nthat project and tenant. The provider has service-wide data access; callers are\nnot granted project access by the provider adapter itself.\n\nThe local provider implements its entire identifier interpretation here. It does\nnot forward requests to an unknown network provider. Native filesystems, symbolic\nlinks and HTTP redirects are not involved. The public module supports separately\nconstructed local clients; the default registry remains the caller-facing API.\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EKksPq3yrda1yqYsH65ZFh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
